   "case_id": "unsupported-wildcard-value",
   "question": "Check the chip-value tool using the full model for GW9 only. Can it calculate the expected points gain from playing my Wildcard?",
   "answer": "**Short answer: no — the chip-value tool does not produce a Wildcard value at all.** It returned only three chips for GW9.\n\n**Chip values (model: `full`, horizon: 1 GW → GW9 only)**\nSnapshot `20261028_212650_step17-current`, as of 2026-10-28, target GW9.\n\n| Chip | GW9 estimated gain | Best GW | Best gain |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Triple Captain | 5.88 | 9 | 5.88 |\n| Bench Boost | 5.24 | 9 | 5.24 |\n| Free Hit | 7.90 | 9 | 7.90 |\n| **Wildcard** | **not returned** | — | — |\n\nThere is no `wildcard` entry in the tool's `values` or `best_gws` output, so no expected-points figure exists for playing it.\n\n**Corroboration from the recommendation tool** (same model, GW9): the Wildcard option is listed with `gain_now: null`, `best_gw: null`, `best_gain: null` and the reason *\"Manual review: Wildcard is not valued.\"* The overall `chip_decision.action` is **`save`** — i.e. no valued chip is recommended for GW9, and the Wildcard remains explicitly unassessed rather than being valued at zero.\n\n**Why this happens:** Wildcard has no automatic value because it depends on how you re-shape the squad (which players you buy and sell, and at what prices), and the chip-value tool holds the squad fixed — it assumes the current squad in every GW with no transfers planned. Only chips that work off a fixed squad can be scored directly. The Free Hit is scored here only because it changes then restores the squad within a single GW; the tool flags that it still \"needs transfer-plan review\".\n\n**Practical next step:** if you want a Wildcard assessment, it has to come through the transfer planner (regular transfer recommendation for GW9 currently shows a gain of 4.96 with `make_transfers: true`, using 3 buys and 3 sells). You can still spend the Wildcard yourself — with £1.1m bank, 3 free transfers and all four chips unused and available until GW19, there's no penalty for holding it.\n\nOne inconsistency worth flagging: Bench Boost shows **5.24** in the chip-value tool but **11.18** in the recommendation's chip options for GW9. That's because the two use different squad bases — the chip-value tool scores your current frozen squad, whereas the recommendation's chip block scores the post-transfer selected XI/bench (Kelleher, Van Hecke and Thiago in, Calafiori, João Pedro and Dubravka out).\n\nAll figures above are model estimates from a frozen snapshot, not guaranteed points.",
