   "answer": "**Arsenal (team ID 1) — GW9 only** (snapshot as of 28 Oct 2026, 2026-27 season, target GW 9)\n\n| Detail | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Opponent | Liverpool (away) |\n| Clean-sheet probability | **28.4%** (0.2836) |\n| Estimate source | `ratings` (ratings-based model) |\n| Supporting xG | Arsenal 1.53 for / 1.26 against |\n\n**Is the clean sheet guaranteed?** No. A 28.4% probability is roughly a one-in-three chance — it is an estimate, not a certainty. A clean sheet also depends on the keeper's save-making, so the rating-derived probability can under- or over-state the realised outcome in any given week.\n\nIf you're weighing a clean-sheet-based play (e.g. an Arsenal defender, or a Liverpool attacker as a differential), this fixture suggests only a modest clean-sheet case, so treat defender value here as more about set-piece/assist upside than a likely clean sheet.",
