   "case_id": "supported-chip-gains",
   "question": "Using the full model for GW9 only, what gains does the chip-value tool estimate for Triple Captain, Bench Boost and Free Hit? Which has the largest estimate? Are these guaranteed extra points?",
   "answer": "**Chip-value estimates (full model, GW9 only, horizon = 1)**\n\nSnapshot: 2026-10-28, target GW9 (deadline 2026-10-31 11:00 UTC), season 2026-27, squad \"[team name]\" (based on GW8).\n\n| Chip | Estimated gain (GW9) |\n|---|---|\n| Triple Captain | 5.88 points |\n| Bench Boost | 5.24 points |\n| Free Hit | 7.90 points |\n\n**Largest estimate:** Free Hit, at roughly 7.9 points — ahead of Triple Captain (~5.9) and Bench Boost (~5.2). The tool's `best_gws` also picks GW9 as the best gameweek for each of these three under a 1-GW horizon.\n\n**No — these are not guaranteed points.** They are model-based hypothetical estimates of *extra* points over and above your current starting XI's projected output (the tool puts your XI at 45.6 expected points for GW9). Actual returns depend on real-world performance, minutes, injuries and fixture outcomes. The tool also notes values are hypothetical even for chips that may no longer be usable, and assumes the current frozen squad in every GW with no transfers planned.\n\n**A few caveats worth flagging:**\n\n- These figures are the chip-value tool's standalone numbers. The recommendation tool's `chip_decision` returns different `gain_now` values for the same chips (3xc 5.88, bboost 11.18, freehit 3.84), because it evaluates over GW9–19 with the selected squad carried forward.\n- On that longer horizon the recommendation's action is **save** — no chip this GW. It plans Triple Captain for GW16 (~6.98), Bench Boost for GW11 (~12.33) and flags Free Hit for GW14 (~10.29) subject to transfer-plan review, since Free Hit changes and then restores the squad. Wildcard is unassessed (not valued).\n- Chip gains are separate from the starting-XI projection and from the transfer objective. The transfer plan for GW9 is separate again: buy Kelleher, Thiago and Van Hecke; sell Calafiori, João Pedro and Dubravka; captain Haaland — expected 49.7 points, a gain of 4.96 over holding.\n\nDon't add the chip gains on top of each other or on top of the 49.7 — they are alternative scenarios for the same gameweek.",
